# MZO Reports — follow the developer guide

Read and follow [DEVELOPER.md](DEVELOPER.md) before changing portals, auth, scope, DataHub, or `sw.js`.

## Must follow

- Login office scope is `mzo_scope.js` (`window.MzoScope`) only. Do not add Office Prefs.
- After loading rows: `MzoScope.filterRows`. Locked selects show the office name, not “All …”.
- Load report CSVs through `mzo_data_hub.js` (`waitForDataset` / `get`). Do not fetch a Google Sheet from the page if a `DATASETS` key exists. Versions skip the body download when unchanged.
- Bump `CACHE_NAME` in `sw.js` and add the page to `isNetworkFirstPath` when HTML/JS must reach users.
- Mobile sticky headers: one compact row (~42–48px); filters as overlay, not a frozen stack.
- New folders need a `vercel.json` static build entry.
- Push `main` to **both** GitHub remotes (`origin` = UtilityDD/mzo_report_pwa, `smartlineman` = smartlinemanapp/mzo-reports). Production is **only** https://mzo-reports.vercel.app. The old `mzo-report-pwa.vercel.app` host redirects in client/SW code; do not add a `vercel.json` catch-all redirect. Do not keep deploying new features to `--scope dipankar-das-projects-1592747b`.

## Keep the guide current

If you add a portal, dataset, API, auth field, scope rule, or a UI pattern others should copy, update `DEVELOPER.md` in the same change.
